<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>opencode2</id>
    <version>2.2.7</version>
    <packageSourceUrl>https://github.com/mu88/chocolatey-packages/tree/main/_auto/opencode2</packageSourceUrl>
    <title>OpenCode 2</title>
    <owners>mu88</owners>
    <authors>Anomaly</authors>
    <copyright>Copyright (c) 2025 - 2026 opencode</copyright>
    <projectUrl>https://opencode.ai/</projectUrl>
    <licenseUrl>https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/dev/LICENSE</licenseUrl>
    <iconUrl>https://opencode.ai/favicon.svg</iconUrl>
    <docsUrl>https://opencode.ai/v2/docs/</docsUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <tags>opencode ai coding agent cli</tags>
    <summary>OpenCode 2 is an open-source AI coding agent.</summary>
    <description>Installs the official OpenCode 2 Windows x64 release and exposes it as opencode2.

Package parameters:
- /AddOpenCodeShim: Also expose OpenCode 2 as opencode. The parameter is optional and disabled by default; /AddOpenCodeShim:false is also accepted. This replaces any existing opencode shim, including OpenCode 1. A previously created shim remains across upgrades and is removed when this package is uninstalled.

Separate commands do not isolate user data: OpenCode 1 and 2 share configuration locations, and OpenCode 2 can migrate terminal settings to cli.json on first launch. The OpenCode project recommends removing a package-managed V1 installation before installing V2. Back up your V1 setup and read https://opencode.ai/v2/docs/migrate-v1 before migrating.

Use Chocolatey to update this package. The standard x64 release requires a compatible processor.</description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/releases</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
